{"id": "DfvTDZmgT0x", "title": "Video by equestralign", "description": "“Heels down!” …a frase from Equestrian nightmares..💀\n\nBut if keeping your heels down feels like a full time job, your ankle mobility could be part of the picture 👀\n\nDorsiflexion is the movement that brings the top of your foot towards your shin. In the stirrup, it helps you let your heel sit below your toes while keeping contact with the ball of your foot. 🦶🔗\n\nIf that movement is limited, you might compensate by gripping with your knees, lifting your heel or shifting your leg forwards. Sometimes another reminder to push your heels down only gets you so far 😅\n\nYour ankles also need to MOVE with your horse. Alongside your hips and knees, they help absorb movement so your lower leg can stay more adaptable rather than rigid. 🐎\n\nWe aren’t trying to force the heels as low as possible. We want to have enough mobility and control for your heel to settle naturally without bracing 💪✨\n\nPosition, stirrup length and tension can play a part too, but those little ankle joints deserve some attention outside the saddle 👀\n\n#equestrianfitness #dressagerider #showjumping #deepcore #Mobility", "channel": "equestralign", "uploader_id": "11880312773", "uploader": "Alice | Equestrian Personal Trainer", "timestamp": 1794696128, "like_count": 698, "comment_count": 1, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1097823759737347a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 62.45, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fayt5-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNtaahmcdM8zfcj-91L57b2y-aoq6thiOLyGmU9wOOeTi3XxzRfejaj7RvECH-VjBLQpBVJAGtcqh0kH92gjJ1zcIwGQDFrqpixibs.mp4?_nc_cat=104&_nc_oc=AdqcFOgPSRwE6czxrK_q0T4QE2nKFqUB_-r8EOFHEYuRMPqVS3mkHGeUkmdHZtUtyks&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fayt5-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=t394FAc0tIYQ7kNvwGrn38Z&&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=oeKz2NmHuqAfmH6WY2biHA&_nc_ss=7b689&_nc_ma